From f764033533bef83b7daa301bf7fd2ee2edea3e8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:57:35 +0000
Subject: software_isp: Sharpen the luma on the cells path

Add the Sharpen IPA algorithm, from the vendor tuning's adaptive spatial
filter (asf32): its gains by gain region, level and activity, and its
clamps. The GPU debayer's cells path takes the luma difference between the
filtered pixel and the mean of the taps around it, after the tone curve, as
the detail, and adds it back scaled by them. The cells path now also runs
when only sharpening is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
